  "problem": "The values of functions $h(t)$ and $z(t)$ and their derivatives at $t=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $h(t)$ | $z(t)$ | ${h}^{′}(t)$ | ${z}^{′}(t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n\nIf $f(t)=\\frac{2h(t)-5}{1-z(t)},$ compute ${f}^{′}(4).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{′}(4)=$\n{{field-1}}",
